Create a function `consecutive_subsequence/1` that accepts a list of integers and returns `true` if the list contains at least one subsequence of consecutive numbers of length three or more. A consecutive subsequence means the numbers are strictly increasing and each is exactly one greater than the previous. The function must handle empty or short lists by returning `false`.

